From 0c35da6d791f5cd72b97ef2cf7a24ac0ceacfe98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:58:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 09/29] fix(snow): route sin/cos/pow through fdlibm; fix stale
 newton log assertion

src/effects/snow.cpp's hand-written custom_adapter kernel (sine(),
cosine(), and the limiter_mask pow call) was still calling bare
std::sin/std::cos/std::pow. That's a real hole in the V8-exact math lane
(intended change (a)): every other call site was migrated to
noisemaker::fdlibm during that pass, but this hand-ported adapter
predates it and was missed. tests/test_no_raw_transcendentals.py is the
enforcement gate for exactly this, and it caught it. Switched all three
calls to noisemaker::fdlibm::sin/cos/pow (already reachable via the
transitively-included noisemaker/fdlibm.hpp). Rebuilt and reran the native
suite: snow_kernel_matches_the_frozen_authority_oracle_byte_for_byte and
the other two snow_kernel_* tests still pass byte-for-byte, confirming
fdlibm agrees with the frozen V8-derived oracle (as expected -- fdlibm
exists to match V8, std:: does not).

tests/test_newton_emitter_lowering.py's
test_emits_authenticated_struct_array_out_and_log_lanes asserted
rendered.count("std::log(") == 2 and rendered.count("std::log2(") == 1.
The actual emission (verified against the live render_typed_cpp output)
uses glsl::log()/glsl::log2(), which dispatch to noisemaker::fdlibm, never
bare std::log/std::log2 -- same fdlibm-lane class as the earlier
mandelbrot/fractal fixes. Updated the counts accordingly (0 std::log(y/log2(,
2 glsl::log(, 1 glsl::log2().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
